    "id": "def_enable_tamper_hardening",
    "name": "Enable Early Launch Anti-Malware Boot Protection",
    "description": "Sets the ELAM boot driver policy to 'good and unknown', so drivers already flagged as malicious are refused before the rest of the system starts. Value 3 (the Windows default) still loads known-bad drivers if they are marked boot-critical; this uses 1, which does not.",
